          "content": "**Page no. 194 Section 8.2 Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.219,
            0.863,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": "Draw a rectangle & then leave one dot distance diagonally to place the four smaller squares. **Q.2. Identify if there are any squares in this collection. Use measurements if needed.** Ans. A is a square."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.318,
            0.878,
            0.375
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "嶽 Think: Is it possible to reason out if the sides are equal or not, and if the angles are right or not without using any measuring instruments in the above figure? Can we do this by only looking at the position of corners in the dot grid?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.383,
            0.861,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Yes, In the above figure without measuring one can reason out for equal sides & right angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.428,
            0.7,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": "Yes, the position of the points on the grid paper makes it possible"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.455,
            0.869,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. Draw at least 3 rotated squares and rectangles on a dot grid. Draw them such that their corners are on the dots. Verify if the squares and rectangles that you have drawn satisfy their respective properties.**"
